 5. **Compatibility and rollout.** Existing browser clients and reusable manual validation assets must request explicit permissions before the stricter BAS is promoted. Any client relying on omission or silent narrowing will receive an error; this is an intentional contract break. Correct BMA documentation/comments separately without deleting its defence-in-depth checks of the permissions actually granted.

 **Consequences:** BAS owns the issuance/API/OpenAPI/test changes; the canonical browser-resource authority record §10.4 is aligned with this amendment. Consumer services retain endpoint-specific authorisation and independent introspection checks. This documentation change authorises no remote push, shared-environment test, deployment, or infrastructure change.
