+<a id="decision-pkb74-event-recovery"></a>
+## 2026-11-01 — Separate PKB command and domain-event recovery
+
+**Status:** Proposed for [PKB #74](https://github.com/Bio-Compass/pkb-service/issues/74); requires architecture review. Extends the existing async failure-observability and idempotency standards without amending accepted BAS authority or platform ownership decisions.
+
+**Proposal:** PKB command ingress and post-commit domain events have separate dead-letter and restricted operator replay paths. An enrichment event must never be recovered through the command-processing pipeline. Replay retains the event identity and passes through the existing transactional workflow/deduplication boundary. There is no automatic dead-letter replay loop, and the runtime producer identity cannot publish to operator replay topics.
+
+PKB owns payloads, failure routing, consumer behavior and the [service-local recovery contract](https://github.com/Bio-Compass/pkb-service/blob/codex/pkb-74-domain-event-dlt/docs/kafka-command-ingress.md#domain-event-failure-recovery-74). The Helm/platform owner owns production topic provisioning, matching partitions, replication/retention and directed broker credentials/ACLs. Review of this proposal or service source does not authorize deployment or establish runtime readiness.
+
+**Evidence and non-goals:** The implementation is tracked by PKB #74. This proposal makes no completed-test or deployment claim. It does not add an enrichment workflow, change authorization ownership, resolve outbox ordering, or authorize automatic migration of historical mixed DLT records.
